BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261007T193000Z
DTEND:20261007T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20261007T000000Z
SUMMARY:Computer Classes at Main Library
DESCRIPTION:UNC’s School of Information and Library Science students and 
 Durham County Library have teamed up to provide a series of workshops on 
 computer skills!\n\nThe Community Workshop Series offers basic technology 
 and computer classes. Classes are free to the general public. You can 
 attend all the classes or just the ones on the skills you would like to 
 work on. Stop by for one on one tech help during a drop in tech help 
 session. Computers are provided for use during class or bring your own 
 device!\n\n \n\n\n\nThird Floor Computer Lab\n\nMain Library\n\n300 North 
 Roxboro Street \n\nWednesdays\n\n3:30 pm - 4:30 pm\n\n \n\n\n\nParking is 
 available in the library lot or for free at the North Queen Street Garage 
 which is located at 115 North Queen street which is located directly across 
 the street from the library behind the apartments. Bring your parking 
 ticket to a service point for validation. \n\n\n\nMore questions? Call 
 919-560-9311\n\n \n\n\n\nSchedule of Classes\n\nSeptember 16 – 
 Intermediate Internet Skills\n\nBuild on the basics and advance to 
 intermediate internet skills!\n\n\n\nSeptember 23  – Drop in Tech 
 Help\n\nOne on one help with a device or computer skill!\n\n\n\nOctober 7 
 – Microsoft Excel Basics\n\nLearn tips and tricks for Microsoft 
 Excel!\n\n\n\n\n\nOctober 14 - Drop in Tech Help\n\nOne on one help with a 
 device or computer skill!\n\n\n\nOctober 28 - Intro to Canva \n\nLearn tips 
 and tricks for Canva!   \n\n\n\nNovember 4 - Online Job Search 
 Basics\n\nLearn how to search and apply for jobs online!\n\n\n\n \n
LOCATION:Computer Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Megan Koslofsky":MAILTO:mkoslofsky@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Career Development, Computer Class, Digital/Tech Literacy, Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-17524047
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17524047
END:VEVENT
