BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261009T143000Z
DTEND:20261009T151500Z
DTSTAMP:20261009T000000Z
SUMMARY:Japanese Paper Arts: Somegami (Fold & Dye Paper)
DESCRIPTION:Designed for parents and children to explore paper arts 
 together\, but all are welcomed! This hands-on program introduces the art 
 of Some-gami\, traditional Japanese fold-and-dye paper craft! In this 
 hands-on class\, participants will fold paper small\, dip the corners in 
 color\, and unfold to reveal unique geometric patterns. Some-gami is 
 related to shibori\, an old Japanese fabric-dyeing 
 method.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFriday\, October 9\, 2026\n\n10:30-11:15 
 a.m.\n\n\n\nMaker Lab at Durham County Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St.\, 
 Durham\, NC)\n\nRegistration preferred \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAdditionally\, 
 the JOI teacher will introduce Japanese sports day events and school life 
 during the class.\n\n\n\nThis is Session 1 of 2 Japanese paper art classes 
 offered this morning. You are welcome to attend 1 or both sessions! If you 
 would also like to join the Chiri-e (Torn Paper Art) class from 11:30 AM 
 – 12:30 PM\, click here to view and register for Session 2.\n\n 
 \n\n\nPresented in partnership with the Japan-America Society\, Japan 
 Outreach Initiative (JOY) Program\, UNC Wilmington\, Tenma Tabi Japan\, and 
 Durham County Library Humanities.\n\n \n\n-\n\n\nInformation on Entering 
 Main Library\n\nParking is available in the library parking lot or at the 
 North Queen Street Garage located at 115 North Queen Street which is behind 
 the apartments directly across the street from the library.
LOCATION:MakerLab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Celeste Holtzmann":MAILTO:choltzmann@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Classes & Lectures, Humanities
UID:LibCal-14288-17629675
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17629675
END:VEVENT
