SUMMARY:Storytime @ the Hub Farm
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for a seasonal-themed storytime at the beautiful 
 Hub Farm!  \n\nThe Hub Farm is a 30-acre outdoor learning center located at 
 117 Milton Road\, Durham\, NC 27712 (adjacent to North Regional Library). 
 For more information\, please visit their website at 
 https://www.thehubfarm.org/. \n\nDirections: From downtown Durham take 
 Roxboro Road north to the stoplight at Milton Road. Turn left and continue 
 past Eno Valley Elementary. Immediately after the school look for signs to 
 the Hub Farm on your left. Parking is available in the Hub Farm Visitor 
 Parking lot\, which is in the Eno Valley Elementary bus lot. \n\nThere is a 
 paved path down to the event area\, which is a covered pavilion area. While 
 some seating is available\, we recommend bringing your own blankets or 
 chairs and to wear comfortable clothing. Afterward\, please feel free to 
 stay and explore the farm!\n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or 
 needs\, please contact Molly at mschaefer@dconc.gov. We ask that all 
 requests be made at least three (3) business days prior to the event to 
 ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible!\n\nThis storytime 
 will be held outside\, weather permitting. If it is raining\, a 
 cancellation notice will be posted on Durham County Library - DCoL Events & 
 Room Reservations - Durham County Library (libcal.com).  Or\, if you are 
 unsure of the status\, please call 919-560-0236 morning-of to confirm 
 whether it is happening. \n\nRegistration for this event is required. There 
 are a total of 45 seats available. When registering\, please remember to 
 include all people in your party. Due to space limitations\, those who are 
 not registered will be unable to attend.  \n\nQuestions? Please email Molly 
 at mschaefer@dconc.gov.  Thank you!
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Molly Schaefer":MAILTO:mschaefer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Story Time
UID:LibCal-14288-17592391
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17592391
END:VEVENT
