SUMMARY:Genealogy Research from the Ground Up
DESCRIPTION:Join the Durham County Library's North Carolina Collection 
 staff to discover basic tools for starting your family history journey. 
 This beginner-friendly workshop will use a case study to demonstrate how 
 you can get your research off the ground. While the case study focuses on 
 North Carolina\, workshop skills can be applied to any U.S. 
 research.\n\nWhat you will learn:\n\n\n	First Steps: How to begin your 
 search and stay organized.\n	How to Find Records: An introduction to basic 
 genealogy records and how to find them\n	Ancestry Library Edition: Tips for 
 searching and a brief introduction to FamilySearch.org\n	Common Pitfalls: 
 How to avoid the most frequent mistakes that trip up researchers\n	Library 
 Resources: An overview of the resources and assistance available in the 
 North Carolina Collection\n\n\nThe session will include a live walkthrough 
 of a real family tree from one of our staff members. You will see firsthand 
 how to apply these research steps to uncover your own history.\n\nIf you 
 have questions about accessibility\, program stimulation levels\, and/or 
 need disability accommodations\, please contact us at 919-560-8593.
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Carmen Ruth":MAILTO:cruth@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17287004
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17287004
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261012T223000Z
DTEND:20261012T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20261012T000000Z
SUMMARY:Climate Up Close
DESCRIPTION:Climate Up Close works to inform and elevate the national 
 conversation on climate change by explaining the scientific consensus 
 clearly\, without partisanship or policy prescriptions. They challenge both 
 denialism and fatalism—the opposing extremes that too often distort 
 climate discourse. Their team of working climate scientists travels to 
 communities across the country so that people can see the evidence for 
 themselves and put their questions directly to researchers. Each event 
 features a 45-minute talk that maps the landscape of climate knowledge\, 
 sorting impacts like heat waves\, sea level rise\, and hurricanes along a 
 spectrum from well understood to genuinely uncertain. Following the talk\, 
 there is an extended Q&A and time to chat with the scientists 
 one-on-one.\n\nRegistration requested\, but walk-ins are welcome!
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jana Bradley":MAILTO:jbradley@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Environmental, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-17456224
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17456224
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261012T223000Z
DTEND:20261012T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20261012T000000Z
SUMMARY:Mystery Book Club -- The Woman in the Window
DESCRIPTION:Join us virtually or in-person to discuss The Woman in the 
 Window by A.J. Finn.\n\nIt isn't paranoia if it's really happening... Anna 
 Fox lives alone -- a recluse in her New York City home\, drinking too much 
 wine\, watching old movies... and spying on her neighbors. Then the 
 Russells move next door: a father\, a mother\, their teenaged son. The 
 perfect family. But when Anna sees something she shouldn't\, her world 
 begins to crumble -- and its shocking secrets are laid bare. What is real? 
 What is imagined? Who is in danger? Who is in control? In this gripping 
 Hitchcockian thriller\, no one and nothing are what they seem.\n\nClick 
 below for format availability:\n\nDurham County\n\nOrange County\n\nChatham 
 County\n\nWake County\n\nAdditionally\, there will be physical copies 
 available at the North Regional Information Desk while supplies 
 last.\n\nRegistration is required to receive the Zoom link to attend the 
 event.\n\nE-mail Bob with any questions: rskesler@dconc.gov
LOCATION:North Regional - Children's Programming Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Bob S.":MAILTO:rskesler@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-16995462
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16995462
END:VEVENT
