BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261013T140000Z
DTEND:20261013T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20261013T000000Z
SUMMARY:Medicare 101
DESCRIPTION:Medicare is a big deal for our community. Nearly 70 million 
 Americans rely on Medicare\, and understanding it helps Durham County 
 families avoid missed enrollment windows\, coverage gaps\, and surprise 
 bills.\n\nThe 4 Parts of Medicare\, simplified. Part A covers hospital 
 care\, Part B covers doctor visits and outpatient care\, Part C (Medicare 
 Advantage) bundles A and B (often with D)\, and Part D covers prescription 
 drugs.\n\nPart D just got a major overhaul. As of 2025\, the prescription 
 drug "donut hole" is gone for good\, and out-of-pocket drug costs are now 
 capped at $2\,000 (2025) / $2\,100 (2026) per year.\n\nTurning 65 starts a 
 7-month enrollment window. Missing this Initial Enrollment Period can mean 
 permanent\, lifelong penalties on Part B and Part D premiums\, so timing 
 matters.\n\nChoosing the right care network matters locally. Comparing Duke 
 Health vs. UNC Health\, and Oak Street Health vs. CenterWell\, helps 
 residents pick a plan that keeps their preferred doctors in-network and 
 fits their transportation and care needs.
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Natalie Killion":MAILTO:nkillion@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Finance, Health & Fitness
UID:LibCal-14288-17605595
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17605595
END:VEVENT
