BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261013T200000Z
DTEND:20261013T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20261013T000000Z
SUMMARY:Why are Katmai's bears so fat? [VIRTUAL ONLY]
DESCRIPTION:This event listing is for the virtual session ONLY.\n\nFor the 
 in-person session\, please visit: 
 https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17615931\n\n\nFat Bear Week 
 devotees\, assemble! \n\nJoin us for a live (virtual) program with a Katmai 
 National Park and Preserve ranger to learn about the ecosystem of the 
 Brooks River inside Alaska's Katmai National Park and Preserve. This 
 mile-long stretch of water supports sockeye salmon\, a keystone species. 
 These fish are the secret to the success for not only the birds and mammals 
 that call this area home\, but also the trees and plants along the 
 riverbank. \n\nThe ranger will talk about the ecosystem and take questions 
 for about 30 minutes. \n\nThis program is geared toward tweens and older\, 
 but younger patrons are welcome too! Best for elementary-age and up.\n\n 
 \n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, please 
 contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be made at 
 least 2 business days prior to the event to ensure we can provide the best 
 accommodations possible.
LOCATION:Virtual
ORGANIZER;CN="Jana Bradley":MAILTO:jbradley@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Environmental, Sensory Friendly, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-17616246
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17616246
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261013T200000Z
DTEND:20261013T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261013T000000Z
SUMMARY:Employment Essentials - Digital Navigation Basics
DESCRIPTION:\na {\n    text-decoration: none\;\n    color: #464feb\;\n}\ntr 
 th\, tr td {\n    border: 1px solid #e6e6e6\;\n}\ntr th {\n    
 background-color: #f5f5f5\;\n}\n\n\n\nPart of the Employment Essentials 
 workshop series\, this beginner‑friendly session introduces adults to the 
 essential building blocks of navigating the online world with confidence. 
 Designed especially for individuals ages 35-60 who have limited experience 
 with computers or the internet\, this workshop provides practical\, 
 easy‑to‑understand guidance in a supportive 
 environment.\n\nParticipants will learn:\n\n\n	What the internet is and how 
 it works in everyday life\n	How to use a web browser to visit 
 websites\n	How search engines help you find information\n	Tips for creating 
 strong\, secure passwords\n	Simple best practices for staying safe 
 online\n\n\nBy the end of this session\, attendees will feel more 
 comfortable using the internet and will be better prepared for digital 
 tasks involved in job searching\, communication\, and everyday online 
 activities.\n\n \n\nAttend 3 sessions of this workshop series to earn a 
 free headshot photo from a professional photographer.
LOCATION:Bragtown Branch Library (3200 Dearborn Dr)
ORGANIZER;CN="Austin Daniels":MAILTO:ausdaniels@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Career Development, Digital/Tech Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-17363761
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17363761
END:VEVENT
