BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261013T220000Z
DTEND:20261013T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20261013T000000Z
SUMMARY:Climate Whiplash: Extreme Weather Explained
DESCRIPTION:This summer in North Carolina we have been yanked back and 
 forth between extreme drought and torrential downpours. Our temperamental 
 weather only seems to be getting more extreme year after year! Have you 
 ever wondered why this is happening and what its long term effects will be 
 on our environment?\n\nJoin Dr. Julianne Davis\, a geologist and climate 
 scientist at UNC's Department of Earth\, Marine and Environmental 
 Sciences\, on Tuesday October 13th from 6:00-7:30p.m.\, in the Innovation 
 Lab to deep dive into the causes and effects of climate whiplash\, and how 
 it relates to our local weather here in Durham. We will have hands on 
 activities\, a presentation as well as time for Q&A! \n\n\n\nRegistration 
 is required\n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or accommodation 
 needs\, please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask that all 
 requests be made at least 2 business days prior to the event to ensure we 
 can provide the best accommodations possible.
LOCATION:Innovation Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kyle Lampart":MAILTO:klampart@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Durham, Environmental, Maker, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-17636962
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17636962
END:VEVENT
