BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261014T170000Z
DTEND:20261014T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
SUMMARY:Daytime Book Club: The House on Mango Street
DESCRIPTION:Come join the Daytime Book Club as we discuss this month's 
 book! New members are always welcome (we love meeting new people!). 
 Registration is appreciated but not required.\n\nThis month we will discuss 
 The House on Mango Street by Sandra Cisneros. The description for the book 
 is below:\n"The House on Mango Street is the remarkable story of Esperanza 
 Cordero\, a young Latina girl growing up in Chicago\, inventing for herself 
 who and what she will become. Told in a series of vignettes-sometimes 
 heartbreaking\, sometimes deeply joyous-Sandra Cisneros' masterpiece is a 
 classic story of childhood and self-discovery. Few other books in our time 
 have touched so many readers."\n\nWe look forward to seeing you all 
 soon!\n\n\nInterested in attending a future Daytime Book Club meeting? Take 
 a look at our reading list below:\n\nMay 2026: To the Lighthouse by 
 Virginia Woolf\n\nJune 2026: The Night Watchman by Louise Erdrich\n\nJuly 
 2026: A Marriage at Sea by Sophie Elmhirst\n\nAugust 2026: My Friends by 
 Fredrik Backman\n\nSeptember 2026: Wild Dark Shore by Charlotte 
 McConaghy\n\nOctober 2026: The House on Mango Street by Sandra 
 Cisneros\n\nNovember 2026: Midnight in the Garden of Good and Evil by John 
 Berendt\n\nDecember 2026: Orbital by Samantha Harvey\n\nJanuary 2027: What 
 We Can Know by Ian McEwan\n\nFebruary 2027: Song of Solomon by Toni 
 Morrison\n\nMarch 2027: Proud Shoes by Pauli Murray\n\nApril 2027: Isola by 
 Allegra Goodman
LOCATION:East Regional - Children's Programming Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Mara Plantholt":MAILTO:mplantholt@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-14288-16576155
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16576155
END:VEVENT
