BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261014T220000Z
DTEND:20261014T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
SUMMARY:Wednesday Computer Class @ Main
DESCRIPTION:Come join a supportive group environment for self-paced digital 
 skills courses. We'll be using Northstar Digital Literacy\, a free online 
 resource available to all Durham County Library patrons. A library staff 
 member will be present to get you set up and answer questions as each 
 participant moves through online modules on their own at their own pace. 
 Northstar allows you to track your learning progress and earn badges or 
 certificates for completing a course. These classes are best for learners 
 who have at least basic keyboard and mouse skills. Our computer lab has a 
 limited number of laptops for use\, so bringing your own laptop and 
 headphones is encouraged.\n\nComputer and digital skills topics 
 include:\n\n\n	Phone Keyboard Basics & Logging In\n	Basic Computer 
 Skills\n	Internet Basics\n	Using Email\n	Windows 10 & 11\n	Mac 
 OS\n	Microsoft Word\, Excel\, and PowerPoint\n	Google Docs\n	Social 
 Media\n	Information Literacy\n	Career Search Skills\n	Your Digital 
 Footprint\n	Accessing Telehealth Appointments\n	Cybersecurity 
 Basics\n\n\nThese classes are self-paced and each week participants will 
 choose which lessons they want to complete on their own. You do not need to 
 have come to the first class to attend the following weeks and there is no 
 requirement to commit to all of the classes through October. Register for 
 the weeks that work best for you!\n\nIf you have any questions or 
 accommodation needs\, contact Jimmy McKinnell at jmckinnell@dconc.gov or 
 call 919-560-9940\n\n\nÚnase a un ambiente de apoyo para cursos de 
 habilidades digitales a su propio ritmo. Usaremos Northstar Digital 
 Literacy\, un recurso en línea gratuito que también está disponible en 
 español para todos los usuarios de la Biblioteca del Condado de Durham. Un 
 miembro del personal de la biblioteca estará presente para ayudarle a 
 comenzar y responder sus preguntas mientras cada participante avanza por 
 los módulos en línea de manera individual y a su propio ritmo. Northstar 
 le permite llevar un registro de su progreso y obtener insignias o 
 certificados al completar un curso. Estas clases son ideales para personas 
 que ya cuentan con habilidades básicas de teclado y mouse. Nuestro 
 laboratorio de computación tiene una cantidad limitada de laptops 
 disponibles\, por lo que se recomienda traer su propio laptop y 
 audífonos.\n\nLos temas de computación y habilidades digitales 
 incluyen:\n\n\n	Conceptos básicos del teclado del teléfono e inicio de 
 sesión\n	Habilidades básicas de computación\n	Conceptos básicos de 
 Internet\n	Uso del correo electrónico\n	Windows 10 & 11\n	Mac 
 OS\n	Microsoft Word\, Excel y PowerPoint\n	Google Docs\n	Redes 
 sociales\n	Alfabetización informacional\n	Habilidades para la búsqueda de 
 empleo\n	Su huella digital\n	Cómo acceder a citas de telesalud\n	Conceptos 
 básicos de ciberseguridad\n\n\nEstas clases son autodirigidas y cada 
 semana los participantes elegirán qué lecciones desean completar por su 
 cuenta. No necesita haber asistido a la primera clase para participar en 
 las siguientes sesiones\, y no es necesario comprometerse a todas las 
 clases hasta octubre. ¡Inscríbase en las semanas que mejor le 
 funcionen!\n\nSi tiene preguntas o necesita alguna adaptación\, 
 comuníquese con Jimmy McKinnell a jmckinnell@dconc.gov o llame al 
 919-560-9940.
LOCATION:Computer Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="James McKinnell":MAILTO:jmckinnell@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Computer Class, Digital/Tech Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-17421738
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17421738
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261014T221500Z
DTEND:20261014T234500Z
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
SUMMARY:Picturebooks Reconsidered: Adults Talking About Picturebooks
DESCRIPTION:Join Jennifer Stone\, PhD\, for a workshop for adults who love 
 picture books. \n\nAny adult (parents\, teachers\, scholars\, etc.) who 
 wants to learn more about picturebooks and how they work is invited join 
 this workshop on picturebook analysis and perspective-taking. We will 
 create a fun and engaging space for learning how to improve critical media 
 literacy skills for ourselves and the children we read with. As a group\, 
 we will read a picturebook\, then discuss common theoretical lenses that 
 can be used to understand it. Then we'll choose a different lens and read 
 the book again to see what we discover! Dr. Stone will draw upon multiple 
 resources including Poetry Unbound\, Five in a Row\, and Media Literacy for 
 Young Children: Teaching Beyond the Screen Time Debates. This will be an 
 interactive workshop\, and patrons are invited to share feelings\, 
 observations\, ideas\, and questions. Each session of the three-part series 
 will explore a different book\, and participants are invited\, but not 
 required\, to attend all three. We welcome you all for an adventure in 
 learning and sharing!\n\n\n\nJennifer Stone\, PhD\, CCC-SLP\n\nJennifer 
 Stone lives in South Durham and owns Stone Circle\, a coaching and 
 consulting practice. Over her 30-year career\, Dr. Stone has advocated for 
 equitable literacy access\, coaching hundreds of educators and parents. She 
 especially loves exploring the many powers of picturebooks with others. Her 
 doctoral research revealed the social power systems embedded in Dolly 
 Parton's Imagination Library and deepened her appreciation of picturebooks 
 as literary works that both reveal and transform cultural expectations. 
 Stone is a mom of two adults\, whom she homeschooled before they went on to 
 graduate from the North Carolina School of Science and Math and NC 
 universities. She loves reading\, dancing\, traveling\, kayaking\, and 
 learning about the natural world.
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Christina Economou":MAILTO:ceconomou@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17640264
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17640264
END:VEVENT
