SUMMARY:Drawn to Graphic Novels: Middle School Book Club @ South Regional
DESCRIPTION:DUE TO THE LIBRARY CLOSURE ON OCT 8\, THIS MEETING HAS BEEN 
 RESCHEDULED FROM THE ORIGINAL DATE TO OCT 12.\n\nThis book club is intended 
 for middle-schoolers in grades 6-8. Meets the 2nd Thursday of each month! 
 ⭐\n\nRead\, share\, sketch\, snack! Discuss great stories\, doodle\, and 
 discover your next favorite graphic novel!\n\n(Stick figures welcome\, but 
 only sketch if you want: no art skills required!)\n\nPlus\, attendees get 
 first pick from books suggested by our Teen Librarian for the next 
 month’s meeting! 📖\n\nThis meeting's theme is Ghost Stories & Cozy 
 Autumn Reads! Kids can prepare by reading any of the titles on this 
 booklist\, or anything else that gives cozy fall vibes\, chills\, or a bit 
 of both! Need some ideas for books to read? Check out this 
 list!\n\n👻🍂🎃🦇🕸️\n\nQuestions? Email Ezra\, South 
 Regional's Teen Librarian\, at eletson@dconc.gov
LOCATION:South Regional - Children's Programming Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Ezra L.":MAILTO:eletson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Social
