BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261017T143000Z
DTEND:20261017T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
SUMMARY:Page & Pen Writing Workshop -- Adaptations: From Book to Big Screen
DESCRIPTION:Grab your notebook and a pen\, and let's write! The Page and 
 Pen Writing Workshop meets roughly every six weeks and is open to anyone 
 who wants to improve their creative writing skills. Session formats vary 
 and may include writing exercises\, discussion about technique and 
 process\, sharing ideas for organizing work sessions and workspaces\, or 
 exploration of any challenges you may be facing in the struggle to 
 write.\n\nThis session: Adaptations -- From Book to Big Screen. Why is the 
 book always better than the movie? Or wait\, is it? Are there movies that 
 outshone the book or short story? Writers face unique challenges when 
 adapting a written story for the screen. What to change? What to add? What 
 to leave out? Most of us have watched movies that veered far enough from 
 the original story or book to cause agitation\, maybe even a bit of anger. 
 Bring your opinions to this meeting\, and let's get into it!\n\nThis 
 program is open to anyone at any time: drop in once\, attend every 
 session\, or show up every once in a while -- no long-term commitment is 
 required. Space is often limited\, so please register in 
 advance.\n\nContact Bob with any questions: rskesler@dconc.gov
LOCATION:North Regional - Children's Programming Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Bob S.":MAILTO:rskesler@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Literacy, Writing
UID:LibCal-14288-17178522
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17178522
END:VEVENT
