BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261017T150000Z
DTEND:20261017T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
SUMMARY:Elevenses\, Coloring\, and The Two Towers
DESCRIPTION:Gather\, good folk\, and spend a fair and merry afternoon in 
 gentle cheer and quiet delight. Come partake of humble refreshments as you 
 lose yourselves in the noble artistry of Lord of the Rings coloring books\, 
 bringing to life the realms of Middle-earth with your own hand.\n\nWhilst 
 we color\, The Lord of the Rings: The Two Towers shall play before us in 
 its full extended glory\, a grand tale unfolding over approximately three 
 hours and fifty-five minutes. The film is rated PG-13.\n\nEach traveler who 
 joins our fellowship shall depart with their own Lord of the Rings coloring 
 book and a set of colored pencils\, so that the spirit of Middle-earth may 
 journey home with them.\n\nRegistration is required to secure your place in 
 this gathering.\n\nFor your presence\, you will earn an extra entry into 
 the One Walk to Rule Them All grand prize drawing with submission of a 
 completed tracker.\n\nThis program is made possible through the generosity 
 of the Friends of the Durham Library.
LOCATION:Adult Programming Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jessica L.":MAILTO:jllundin@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Friends of the Durham Library, Movie, One Walk
UID:LibCal-14288-16306035
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16306035
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261017T160000Z
DTEND:20261017T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
SUMMARY:Duke Ballet & Books
DESCRIPTION:Duke Ballet & Books is a group of Duke University student 
 volunteers who run free arts and literacy programming for 6-9 year 
 olds.\n\nThere are two parts to every Ballet & Books session:\n\n1. 
 45-minute ballet class where students learn choreography to perform at an 
 end-of-semester showcase.\n2. 45-minute reading mentorship session where 
 mentors and students read together and do related activities aimed at 
 helping build literacy skills.\n\nTo learn more and register\, contact 
 duke@balletandbooks.org\n
LOCATION:Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Christina Economou":MAILTO:ceconomou@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-17325510
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17325510
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261017T161500Z
DTEND:20261017T181500Z
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
SUMMARY:Open Sew with Connecting with Threads
DESCRIPTION:This class is geared towards tweens and teens who already know 
 how to sew and/or have completed 12 weeks of our Learn To Sew program.  In 
 this program\, they will learn how to complete intermediate level projects 
 from start to finish as they expand their knowledge from basic sewing 
 skills to creating complete projects from a pattern. They will also be 
 making a project to give to someone in our community--perhaps a dog blanket 
 or a quilt for a baby in the NICU.\n\nThe six programs are scheduled for: 
 August 29\, Sept 12\, Sept. 26\, Oct. 10\, Oct. 17\, and Oct. 24. Many 
 projects will take more than one session to complete\, so be sure to sign 
 up for multiple sessions. For tweens (ages 9 and up) and teens Registration 
 is required! You must register individually for each session you plan to 
 attend.
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline P.":MAILTO:cbpeterson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts
UID:LibCal-14288-17349111
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17349111
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261017T170000Z
DTEND:20261017T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
SUMMARY:Fall Community Plant Swap
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to our Fall Community Plant Swap!\n\nBring and take 
 saplings\, shrubs\, bulbs\, houseplant cuttings\, flowers\, and seeds to 
 swap and share with other local gardeners! Check out free seeds from our 
 Digging Durham Seed Library\, and resources from Master Gardeners with the 
 Cooperative Extension Office! Enjoy the Fall bounty and planting season 
 together! \n\nThe swap will be held on October 17 1:00-3:00 p.m. at the 
 Main Library located at 300 North Roxboro Street\, inside the MakerLab on 
 the first floor.   \n\n \n\nPlease bring your own boxes or bags for 
 transporting plants. A marker\, painters' tape or tags\, and small bags or 
 envelopes are also helpful at plant swaps. \n \n\nParking is available in 
 the library lot or at the North Queen Street Garage (115 North Queen 
 Street) which is located directly across the street from the library behind 
 the apartments. We can validate parking in the garage at the Circulation 
 Desk with your ticket.\n\n\n\nDigging Durham Seed Library \n\nExtension 
 Master Gardener Volunteers of Durham County\n\nRegistration is appreciated 
 to determine the amount of people that might attend and to receive an email 
 reminder about the event.\n\nIf you have any questions\, feel free to 
 contact etyler@dconc.gov
LOCATION:MakerLab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Ethan Tyler":MAILTO:etyler@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Durham, Environmental, Food & Cooking, Gardening, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-17442783
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17442783
END:VEVENT
