BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261017T230000Z
DTEND:20261018T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
SUMMARY:Morbid Tales: A Night of Horror & Heavy Metal
DESCRIPTION:For the fourth time the great Bell Of Doom tolls and Durham 
 County Library once again joins forces with the Horror Writers' Association 
 to conjure a spectacle of dread and sonic nightmare beneath the streets of 
 our fair city. Descend into the subterranean crypt of Moon Dog Meadery for 
 an evening of live horror readings from local authors Richard Dansky\, 
 Rikki Goodwin\, and Jon Carroll Thomas followed by a special performance 
 from Noctomb\, crawling forth from their moldering grave to bring terror 
 and auditory abomination to the souls of Durham. \n\nThis event will be 
 held at Moon Dog Meadery\, located at 1104 Broad St. Admission will be 
 first come\, first serve. Register for more information and a reminder 
 email. \n\nPlease be advised this event may feature disturbing content for 
 mature audiences\n\n \n\nWidely regarded as a leading expert on video game 
 writing and narrative\, Richard Dansky has worked on franchises such as The 
 Division\, Far Cry\, Splinter Cell\, Assassins Creed\, and more. He is the 
 author of The Video Game Writer’s Guide to Surviving an Industry That 
 Hates You\, and co-authored the upcoming horror graphic novel Bridgewater 
 with French comics legend Matz. Richard has published 8 novels and 2 short 
 story collections\, with his next novel\, Nightmare Logic\, scheduled for 
 release in 2026. He has worked extensively in tabletop RPG writing as 
 well\, having been a core contributor to White Wolf’s classic setting The 
 World of Darkness. Richard is also pretty sure he is the only working 
 horror writer to have won PC Gamer Magazine’s coveted “Mission Pack of 
 the Year” award\, and he was briefly the world’s leading expert on 
 Denebian Slime Devils. https://richarddansky.com/\n\nRikki Goodwin is a 
 horror writer living in North Carolina. She has three novels: Lovers’ 
 Leap\, Ghost Glasses\, and Dark Eyes\, and has also contributed stories to 
 several anthologies. Her “real” job is also a fun one\; if she’s not 
 writing or reading\, she’d poking holes in people as a professional body 
 piercer in the tattoo studio she owns.\n\nJon Carroll Thomas is a dark 
 fiction writer\, event coordinator\, and corporate grocery store peon. He 
 lives in a little log house in Raleigh\, North Carolina\, with his 
 beautiful wife\, charming son\, and six spoiled rescue cats. He leads the 
 Quails From The Crypt book club through Quail Ridge Books in Raleigh\, and 
 is a founding member of the North Carolina chapter of the Horror Writers 
 Association. He enjoys vintage cartoons and old movies that take place in 
 creepy\, old houses. His recent stories appear in Whetstone: Amateur 
 Magazine of Pulp Sword and Sorcery\, Cosmic Horror Monthly\, and on the 
 Creepy Podcast.\n\nNoctomb is a three-piece crawling forth from the rotten 
 caverns beneath of Raleigh\, NC. A distinctively southern blend of black\, 
 sludge\, and doom metal\, combining low n' slow riffs with fast ragers. A 
 sonic journey into putrid realms of woe and annihilation. \n\n
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Larkin Coffey":MAILTO:lcoffey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17642245
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17642245
END:VEVENT
