SUMMARY:Preschool STEAM Storytime: Let's Learn About Bones!
DESCRIPTION:Preschoolers (ages 3-5 years) and their caregivers are welcome 
 to join Ms. Natalie for a STEAM (Science\, Technology\, Engineering\, 
 Arts\, and Mathematics) storytime! On the 1st and 3rd Monday of every 
 month\, we will explore a different STEAM topic with stories\, songs\, and 
 a hands-on activity.\n\nThis week\, we will learn all about our bones and 
 create our own moving skeletons using brass fasteners\, cardstock paper\, 
 crayons\, and hole punchers!\n\nRegistration is required.\n\nIf you have 
 questions about accessibility\, program stimulation levels\, and/or need 
 disability accommodations\, please contact us at (919) 560-8592.
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Natalie Perez":MAILTO:natperez@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, STEAM, Story Time
