SUMMARY:Playdough Playtime (Ages 2-6)
DESCRIPTION:Join us to build and play with our collection of colorful 
 Play-Doh and sculpting toys! This is a fun\, sensory playtime to foster 
 creativity and exploration while building fine motor skills. This program 
 is geared towards children ages 2-6 and their caregivers. \n\nDoes your 
 little one have an allergy to gluten? We can provide kinetic sand and 
 sanitized tools. Please reach out to Kristen at kstockdale@dconc.gov prior 
 to this program for accommodations. \n\nAll supplies provided. Registration 
 is appreciated but not required. \n\n \n\nIf you have questions about 
 accessibility\, program stimulation levels\, and/or need disability 
 accommodations\, please contact us at (919) 560-8592.
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kristen Stockdale":MAILTO:kstockdale@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, Arts & Crafts, High & Low Sensory Stimulation, STEAM
