DTEND:20261023T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261023T000000Z
SUMMARY:Main's Teen Gaming Area
DESCRIPTION:Join the Librarians in the Teen Gaming Area! Come solo or bring 
 your friends! Play various titles for the PlayStation 5 and Nintendo 
 Switch. For Tweens & Teens in Grades 6th – 12th.\n\nPlease Note: Tweens 
 in 5th grade can use the gaming area only if they are accompanied in the 
 area with an adult age 18 and over.\n \n
LOCATION:Main Library - Teen Gaming Area\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="LaShaunda Rogers":MAILTO:lrogers@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17255732
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17255732
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261023T193000Z
DTEND:20261023T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261023T000000Z
SUMMARY:Teen Game Day!
DESCRIPTION:Ready for some friendly competition? Join us for Teen Game 
 Day\, where you can jump into video games\, card games\, and classic board 
 games—all in one place! Whether you’re into fast-paced console 
 battles\, strategy-packed tabletop games\, or quick card challenges with 
 friends\, there’s something for everyone. Come play\, hang out\, and 
 discover your new favorite game in a relaxed\, welcoming space. All skill 
 levels are encouraged\, and all games are provided—just bring your best 
 moves!  If you have any questions or concerns\, please contact Dominique at 
 fdiggs@dconc.gov.\n
LOCATION:North Regional - Children's Programming Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Dominique Diggs":MAILTO:fdiggs@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Gaming
UID:LibCal-14288-16610708
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16610708
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261023T200000Z
DTEND:20261023T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261023T000000Z
SUMMARY:Game On: Nintendo Switch Fun at Bragtown
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Bragtown Branch Library for daily gaming for 
 tweens and teens! Dive into the world of Nintendo Switch with an array of 
 exciting games available for play. Challenge your friends\, explore new 
 worlds\, and level up your gaming skills in a welcoming and inclusive 
 environment. Registration is required. \n\n
LOCATION:Bragtown Branch Library (3200 Dearborn Dr)
ORGANIZER;CN="Felicia Nobles":MAILTO:flnobles@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Digital/Tech Literacy, Gaming, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-17651442
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17651442
END:VEVENT
