SUMMARY:ABC's of Bike Repair with Durham Bike Co-op
DESCRIPTION:Registration required! Register below.\n\nThe Durham Bicycle 
 Cooperative wants to empower people to not only repair their bicycles but 
 keep them in safe working condition. In this free session\, you'll learn 
 the ABCs of bicycle safety: Air\, Brakes\, and Chain. \n\nAir: It's 
 important to keep your tires properly inflated\, know how to change a tube 
 in case you get a flat\, and to check tires regularly for wear.\n\nBrakes: 
 It's important that your brakes are in good condition\, properly adjusted\, 
 brake well\, and that you know how to do minor adjustments that don’t 
 require any tools.\n\nChain: The chain drives the whole bike\, so it's 
 important to check it for wear\, and keep it shifting well. \n\nIf you have 
 any accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, please contact us at 
 Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be made at least 2 business 
 days prior to the event to ensure we can provide the best accommodations 
 possible!
LOCATION:MakerLab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kyle Lampart":MAILTO:klampart@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17635908
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17635908
