SUMMARY:Don't Let Diet Culture Haunt You
DESCRIPTION:Join this empowering workshop designed to help participants 
 break free from confusing food rules and find a sustainable way of eating 
 that genuinely supports their well-being. Together\, we'll explore how 
 guilt-driven restrictions and "perfect or failed" thinking keep people 
 stuck on the diet rollercoaster\, and we'll learn strategies for building a 
 personalized nutrition roadmap based on balance\, realism\, and self-trust. 
 This session encourages attendees to question unhelpful food beliefs\, let 
 go of one-size-fits-all diets\, and adopt an eating style that feels 
 positive\, practical\, and achievable for everyday life. \n\nThis workshop 
 is presented by licensed and registered dietitian Lucy Hayhurst\, founder 
 of Well Balanced Nutrition.
LOCATION:Meeting Room #4347\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Austin Daniels":MAILTO:ausdaniels@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Food & Cooking, Health & Fitness
