DTSTART:20261026T150000Z
DTEND:20261026T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20261026T000000Z
SUMMARY:Computers Basics
DESCRIPTION:Gain valuable computer skills on these topics:\n\nComputer 
 Basics\n\n\n	Using an operating system\; opening programs\; saving\, 
 copying\, and deleting files.\n\n\nDocuments & Typing\n\n\n	Word processing 
 basics\; editing and saving documents\; formatting text\; cut copy and 
 paste.\n\n\nInternet Basics \n\n\n	Browsing websites\; searching with 
 Google\; using online forms\; keeping accounts secure.\n\n\nOnline 
 Life\n\n\n	Avoiding scams\; protecting your privacy\; finding reliable 
 info\; using social media safely.\n\n\nTo sign up: Call 919-293-1133 or 
 click the link to register below:\n\n\n \n\nClass Sign Up Link\n\n\n
LOCATION:SLW Meeting Room - Side 1\, Stanford L. Warren Branch Library (1201 Fayetteville St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Larry Daniels":MAILTO:ldaniels@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17708988
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17708988
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261026T163000Z
DTEND:20261026T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20261026T000000Z
SUMMARY:Computer Classes: Drop-In Tech Help
DESCRIPTION:Need help outside of a class? Want some 1:1 time to figure out 
 your tech? Join us for drop in tech help! We will have instructors from the 
 Community Workshop Series at UNC-CH ready to assist you. Registration 
 strongly encouraged!\n\nThings we can help with:\n\n\n	Using library 
 e-resources (Libby\, Hoopla\, Consumer Reports\, etc)\n	Setting up an email 
 or online account\n	Help filling out an online application\n	Help with 
 using applications like Word\, Excel\, and Google Apps\n\n\nWe cannot help 
 with resume creation. Additionally\, we cannot offer medical\, financial or 
 legal advice. If you need in-depth assistance with job seeking\, we can 
 refer you to Business Services. \n\nThis class is a part of a series of 
 computer classes. See the schedule below:\n\nMonday\, September 28: AI 
 Basics\nMonday\, October 12: Drop-In Tech Help\nMonday\, October 19: Excel 
 101 \nMonday\, October 26: Drop-in Tech Help\nMonday\, November 2: 
 Troubleshoot Your Tech\nMonday\, November 9: Drop-in Tech Help\nMonday\, 
 November 16: Organize Your Photos\, Files\, & More
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Raivynn Smith":MAILTO:raivynnsmith@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, Classes & Lectures, Computer Class, Digital/Tech Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-17494495
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17494495
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261026T180000Z
DTEND:20261026T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261026T000000Z
SUMMARY:Board Game Cafe
DESCRIPTION:Want to try out a new board game? Are you looking to play some 
 classics\, but you're not sure how to find other players to join you? Then 
 come grab a warm beverage\, pick out a game\, and meet others in your 
 community at our Board Game Cafe!\n\nThe Board Game Cafe will provide 
 community members with some warming drinks and a variety of board games to 
 play in the library. The board games 
 include:\n\n\n	Cartographers\n	Codenames\n	Dominion\n	Mysterium\n	One Night 
 Ultimate Werewolf\n	Really Loud Librarians\n	Scrabble\n	Settlers of 
 Catan\n	Splendor\n	Sushi Go\n	Ticket to Ride\n	Trivial 
 Pursuit\n	Uno\n	Villainous\n	Wingspan\n	Yeti In My Spaghetti\n	& 
 more!\n\n\nCommunity members are also welcome to bring snacks and their own 
 favorite board games to share at the event.\n\nRegistration is appreciated 
 but not required.\n\nQuestions? Contact Mara (she/her): 
 mplantholt@dconc.gov.
LOCATION:East Regional - Children's Programming Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Mara Plantholt":MAILTO:mplantholt@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Gaming
UID:LibCal-14288-15962781
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15962781
END:VEVENT
