SUMMARY:Owl-o-ween Owl Pellet Dissection
DESCRIPTION:Happy Owl-o-Ween!\n\nLearn more about these amazing animals by 
 dissecting owl pellets\, the undigested bones\, fur\, and feathers of the 
 owl's prey. (Technically\, these are raptor pellets\, but owl-o-ween is 
 better than raptor-ween!)\n\nComing with friends? Please consider working 
 together so we can welcome more people to this program. Register as 
 "bringing a guest\," but please keep the maximum group size to 
 4!\n\nPellets are locally sourced and sanitized. Nitrile gloves must be 
 worn during dissection.\n\n \n\n \n\nPicture sourced from Barn Owl 
 Trust.\n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, 
 please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be 
 made at least 2 business days prior to the event to ensure we can provide 
 the best accommodations possible.\n\n
LOCATION:MakerLab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
